        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "22a9fe4c-f66e-58cf-94f1-be2bb37734c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Warren G. Harding, Nan Britton, Elizabeth Britton\n- Roles: President of the United States, United States Senator, secretary, mistress\n- Events: Harding presidency, Harding's death, Teapot Dome scandal, paternity revelation\n\nFacts:\n- Warren G. Harding was born on November 2, 1865, and later became the 29th President of the United States.\n- Nanna Popham Britton was born on November 9, 1896, and was an American secretary.\n- Warren G. Harding served in the United States Senate before he was elected president.\n- Warren G. Harding served as the 29th President of the United States from March 4, 1921, until his death in 1923.\n- At the time of his death on August 2, 1923, Warren G. Harding was one of the most popular presidents.\n- After Warren G. Harding's death, scandals from his administration, including Teapot Dome, damaged his reputation.\n- Revelations that Nan Britton had been one of Warren G. Harding's mistresses also damaged Warren G. Harding's reputation.\n- In 1927, Nan Britton said that her daughter Elizabeth had been fathered by Warren G. Harding while he was serving in the United States Senate, one year before he was elected president.\n- Nanna Popham Britton died on March 21, 1991.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
